            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery disease: combined stress MR imaging protocol-one-stop evaluation of myocardial perfusion and function.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>608-14</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors developed and tested a dual stress magnetic resonance (MR) imaging protocol to evaluate myocardial perfusion, function, and hibernation. The technique was well tolerated, and high-quality images were achieved. The comprehensive information obtained can be used to guide clinical management decisions regarding coronary artery revascularization procedures. This protocol offers a one-stop assessment of patients with coronary artery disease with use of a clinical MR imager.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
